# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the user should
#   choose their own version. For an application, you may want to commit them.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1253, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in git.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if the platform is not identical, it may cause dependency resolution issues.
#   Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similarly, Poetry manages poetry.lock and it is recommended to commit it.
#   poetry.lock

# pdm
#   PDM stores project-wide configurations in .pdm.toml
.pdm.toml
.pdm-plugins/

